  <h1>Business Video Production Costs & Process for Swiss Companies</h1>
  <p class="lead">Professional video production is no longer a luxury for Swiss enterprises—it's essential. If you're wondering how much a corporate video costs and what the production process actually involves, the answer depends on scope, duration, and distribution. Most Swiss companies invest CHF 8,000–80,000 for a high-quality [[services/corporate-video|corporate video]], but strategic partnerships with experienced production houses can deliver measurable ROI through increased engagement, brand credibility, and lead generation.</p>
  <p class="post-meta"><span>Sofia Treviño</span> <span>·</span> <span>July 24, 2026</span></p>
</div></div></section>
<section class="sec" style="padding-top:40px"><div class="wrap"><div class="post-wrap post-body reveal">
<img src="/projects/v-zug-combair-600-how-to-video-campaign/03-UG_How_To_Videos_Viven_Video_Agency_12.jpg" alt="Business Video Production Costs & Process for Swiss Companies" loading="eager" style="width:100%;border-radius:16px;margin:8px 0 26px;aspect-ratio:16/9;object-fit:cover" />
<h2>Why Swiss Companies Are Investing in Video</h2><p>Video content drives engagement at three times the rate of static content. Fortune 500 companies, including those headquartered in Switzerland, now allocate 15–25% of marketing budgets to video. The reasons are clear: search engines prioritize video, employees retain 95% of a message when delivered via video versus 10% via text, and decision-makers watch videos before making B2B purchases.</p><p>Swiss companies operate in a premium market segment. Clients expect professional communication, and poor-quality video damages brand perception. Conversely, polished video—whether <a href={p("services/product-video")}>showcasing a product</a> or explaining a complex service—positions your company as serious and trustworthy.</p><h2>What Determines Video Production Costs</h2><p>Video production pricing is not one-size-fits-all. Several factors shape the final invoice:</p><ul><li><strong>Concept and strategy:</strong> Are you working from a detailed brief, or does the production house develop the concept? Custom storytelling costs more than template-based approaches.</li><li><strong>Location and logistics:</strong> Studio production is typically cheaper than on-location shoots. International travel or industrial site filming adds costs.</li><li><strong>Talent:</strong> Professional voice-over artists, actors, or on-camera presenters increase the budget. User-generated content or internal talent reduces it.</li><li><strong>Post-production complexity:</strong> Motion graphics, colour grading, sound design, and multiple revisions add to the timeline and cost.</li><li><strong>Duration:</strong> A 60-second social video costs less than a 5-minute brand documentary. But this also depends on it's content.</li><li><strong>Distribution:</strong> Do you need multiple formats (horizontal, vertical, square) for different platforms? Repurposing content costs extra but maximizes ROI.</li></ul><h2>Typical Budget Ranges for Swiss Businesses</h2><p>Based on thousands of projects across industries:</p><ul><li><strong>Small business (startup, SME):</strong> CHF 8,000–25,000 for a single 2–3 minute video. Often combines stock footage, internal team members, and one day of shooting.</li><li><strong>Mid-market company:</strong> CHF 25,000–60,000 for a series or a premium single video. Includes custom concept, professional talent, multi-day shoot, and full post-production.</li><li><strong>Enterprise:</strong> CHF 60,000–150,000+ for brand campaigns, annual reports, or <a href={p("services/employer-branding")}>employer branding</a> initiatives. May span weeks of production and dozens of revisions.</li><li><strong><a href={p("services/social-media-video")}>Social media content</a> (ongoing):</strong> CHF 3,000–12,000 per month for a managed production partnership.</li></ul><p>Remember: the cheapest option is rarely the best investment. A poorly executed video damages your brand more than no video at all.</p><h2>How Professional Video Production Works</h2><p>A transparent production partner will walk you through these stages:</p><p><strong>1. Discovery and strategy</strong><br>You meet with the creative team to align on goals, audience, and key messages. They ask about your competitors, brand tone, and success metrics. This phase typically lasts 1–2 weeks and is essential for a video that actually converts.</p><p><strong>2. Concept and script</strong><br>Based on the brief, the team develops a creative concept (visual direction, narrative arc, tone) and writes the script. You review and approve revisions. Budget: 2–3 weeks.</p><p><strong>3. Pre-production planning</strong><br>The producer coordinates locations, talent, crew, equipment, and scheduling. Shot lists and storyboards are finalized. A detailed plan avoids costly on-set surprises.</p><p><strong>4. Filming</strong><br>The shoot day (or days) happens. Professional crews handle lighting, sound, camera work, and direction. Most corporate videos require 1–3 shoot days.</p><p><strong>5. Post-production and edit</strong><br>Editors assemble footage, add graphics, sound design, and colour correction. You receive rough cuts for feedback. This phase is where raw footage becomes a polished asset. Typically 2–4 weeks.</p><p><strong>6. Final delivery and optimization</strong><br>The video is exported in multiple formats for web, social, and email. You receive master files and usage guidelines. A strong production partner also advises on distribution strategy.</p><h2>Maximizing ROI on Your Video Investment</h2><p>The video itself is only the beginning. To get the most from your investment:</p><ul><li><strong>Repurpose across channels:</strong> A 5-minute brand story can become 8–10 social clips, email snippets, and presentation segments.</li><li><strong>Optimize for SEO:</strong> Host on your website with proper metadata. <a href={p("services/how-to-video")}>How-to videos</a> in particular drive organic traffic.</li><li><strong>Integrate with sales:</strong> Share with your team and embed in proposals, follow-ups, and landing pages.</li><li><strong>Measure performance:</strong> Track views, completion rates, click-throughs, and conversions. Data guides your next investment.</li></ul><h2>Choosing the Right Production Partner</h2><p>Not every video agency is equipped to serve Swiss enterprise clients. Look for a partner who:</p><ul><li>Has experience in your industry (financial services, manufacturing, pharma, etc.)</li><li>Understands your market and can position your story competitively</li><li>Offers transparent pricing with no hidden fees</li><li>Provides clear timelines and revision policies</li><li>Has a portfolio of work from recognized Swiss and international brands</li></ul><p>Ask for references, review their <a href={p("projects")}>recent work</a>, and schedule a consultation before committing.</p><p>Video production is a long-term asset for your brand. When done right, a professional video generates leads, builds trust, and amplifies your competitive edge in the Swiss market. If you're ready to discuss your video strategy, <a href={p("contact")}>get in touch with our team</a>. We've helped companies like UBS, Siemens, and Porsche translate their vision into impactful content.</p>
